+/// A range of words in one of the pool's word lists, as stored in `Item.data`.
+const ExtraRange = struct {
+    start: u32,
+    len: u32,
+};
+
+/// Checks that `len` more words still fit in the `u32` addressable window of
+/// `list` and reserves capacity for them, returning the offsets the appended
+/// words will occupy.
+///
+/// Every range the pool hands out is addressed as `list[start + i]` with a
+/// `u32` `start`, so a range whose `start + len` does not fit in a `u32` could
+/// no longer address its own last element. That is a limit of the
+/// representation rather than of the allocator, so it is reported as
+/// `error.OutOfMemory` - the error these entry points already return - and
+/// callers keep their current error set. The check runs before any capacity is
+/// reserved or word written, so a rejected append leaves `list` untouched and
+/// never publishes a partial range.
+fn reserveRange(list: anytype, gpa: Allocator, len: usize) error{OutOfMemory}!ExtraRange {
